// Title: Forest Blizzard APT - Custom Protocol Handler Creation
// Sigma ID: 5cdeb555-65de-4767-99fe-e26807465148
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1547.001
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects the setting of a custom protocol handler with the name "rogue". Seen being created by
//   Forest Blizzard APT as reported by MSFT.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2024/04/22/analyzing-forest-blizzards-custom-post-compromise-tool-for-exploiting-cve-2022-38028-to-obtain-credentials/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2024/TA/Forest-Blizzard/registry_set_apt_forest_blizzard_custom_protocol_handler.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\PROTOCOLS\\Handler\\rogue\\CLSID" and RegistryValueData =~ "{026CC6D7-34B2-33D5-B551-CA31EB6CE345}"
